   "author": "Hollowmere team (forest round 4)",
   "population": "hunters",
   "story": "Gideon Kell spent eleven summers pouring a bunker under his cabin on the hill: two levels of concrete, a generator, a year of cans, air filters, a ham set and a blast door. The night the radio said the Cordon had closed the roads, he took Marion and the boys down the shaft under the front-room rug and shot the bolts. The Pruitts from down the hill knew about the bunker. They came up the drive with their grandmother coughing in the truck bed, and Gideon would not open. They found the hatch, forced the storeroom and lived on his cans over his head, and the air intake drew through the storeroom. By spring the filters were furred white with Bloom. Gideon came up the escape tunnel one last night to hunt for spare cartridges, wrote his journal at his desk and went back down to his radio. The spare key to the blast door is still in that desk, where he told his brother-in-law over the radio it would be.",
